ean status per paper is kept in authored/evidence-status.json.","citation_ids":["cite.long.thm-periodic-support"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.thm-periodic-support"],"id":"long.thm-periodic-support","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Theorem 6.20 (Periodic-support irrationality)","locator":"Long record Theorem 6.20, p. 50, label thm:periodic-support","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*Let $b\\ge2$ and $m\\ge1$ be integers. Suppose $A\\subseteq\\mathbb{N}_{>0}$ is nonempty and satisfies $n\\in A$ if and only if $n+m\\in A$ for every $n\\ge1$. Then $X_A(b)$ is irrational.*\n\n*The indicator of $A$ is a nonzero purely periodic integer weight, so this follows from Luca and Tachiya’s theorem stated above. The linked declaration supplies a separate formal proof. At $m=1$ the only nonempty periodic support is full support; residue classes and unions of residue classes give the other immediate examples.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/long.thm-periodic-support","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/long.thm-periodic-support","id":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/edges/%5B%22long.thm-periodic-support%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR20.irrational_erdosSupportSeries_positivePeriodic%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/edges/%5B%22long.thm-periodic-support%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR20.irrational_erdosSupportSeries_positivePeriodic%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR20.irrational_erdosSupportSeries_positivePeriodic"},{"derived":true,"family":"provenance","fro